AD  - Battelle Memorial Institute, Columbus, OH, United States
AD  - U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Research Triangle Park, NC, United States
AB  - The air quality index (AQI) measures how clean or polluted the air is in terms of an associated health risk within a few hours or days after breathing polluted air1. Since PM2.5 federal reference method (FRM) monitors often report data less frequently than daily with a delay of more than a week, continuous PM2.5 monitors may be used to provide more timely AQI reporting, provided a relationship between the continuous and FRM measurements is established by statistical linear regression. This enables agencies to advise the public about the air they are breathing or forecast the air quality so that they can adjust their activities and therefore their exposure. This article descirbes a measure of adequacy for such a relationship and develops regression models for two case studies.
