AB  - The hourly particulate matter (PM) 2.5 concentrations were characterized from four different monitoring sites in EPA region 5, and compares them to Federal Reference Method (FRM). The hourly characterization was done using time series and autocorrelation. The continuous data was compared to FRM by averaging hourly data across 24-hour sampling periods and modelled these averages against their respective daily FRM concentrations. The tapered element oscillating microbalance (TEOM) analysis showed a relationship with season and temperature, linear correlation as low as 0.6308, and nonlinear model correlation as high as 0.8779 when modeled with temperature.
