AB  - The hourly PM 2.5 concentrations measured via a nephelometer at the Mayville, WI EPA Region 5 monitoring site were characterized using time series and auto correlation. This data was then compared to concurrent Federal Reference method (FRM) and Tapered Element Oscillating Microbalance (TEOM) measurements. The hourly value averages are modeled using simple linear least squares regression and more complex regression involving additional meteorological variables such as temperature and relative humidity. The nephelometer analysis shows no discernible annual relationship with time, in contrast to seasonal TEOM variability.
